melody:
# Chorus (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
By the light of the sil-ver-y moon, I want to spoon,
E4/ F4/ G4(4) r C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 A4(4) r D5 C5 A4 B4(4)
to my hon-ey I'll croon love's tune.
r G4/ A4/ B4/ A4/ G4 A4(2) E4(2) G4(2) r
Hon-ey-moon, keep a-shin-ing in June.
E4/ F4/ G4(4) r C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 A4(4)
Your sil-v'ry beams will bring love dreams, we'll be cud-dl-ing soon,
r D5 E5 F5 E5 C5 D5 F5 E5 C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 E5(4)
by the sil-ver-y moon.
r C5/ D5/ E5/ C5/ D5 C5(4) ~C5 r r

# Once more
By the light of the sil-ver-y moon, I want to spoon,
E4/ F4/ G4(4) r C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 A4(4) r D5 C5 A4 B4(4)
to my hon-ey I'll croon love's tune.
r G4/ A4/ B4/ A4/ G4 A4(2) E4(2) G4(2) r
Hon-ey-moon, keep a-shin-ing in June.
E4/ F4/ G4(4) r C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 A4(4)
Your sil-v'ry beams will bring love dreams, we'll be cud-dl-ing soon,
r D5 E5 F5 E5 C5 D5 F5 E5 C5/ D5/ E5/ D5/ C5 E5(4)
by the sil-ver-y moon.
r C5/ D5/ E5/ C5/ D5 C5(4) ~C5 r r r
